oxed{}\\,\\text{d}S,\n$$\n\nwhat is the missing expression?" 13194139534928 17592186045417 true] [17592186167127 1074 "If $S$ is an oriented surface with unit normal vector $n,$ and $F$ is continuous vector field, then the flux of $F$ across $S$ measured with respect to $n$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S.\n$$\n\nCalculating the dot product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F\\cdot n & =⟨2z,\\,x+y,\\,y-z⟩\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}⟨1,\\,-1,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}⟨2z,\\,x+y,\\,y-z⟩\\cdot ⟨1,\\,-1,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}(2z-(x+y)+(y-z)) \\\\  & =\\frac{z-x}{\\sqrt{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the flux can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S \\\\  & ={∬}_{S}\\frac{z-x}{\\sqrt{3}}\\,\\text{d}S \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}{∬}_{S}z-x\\,\\text{d}S.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534928 17592186045417 true] [17592186444600 1043 #edb/ref 17592186444620 13194139534928 17592186045417 true] [17592186444600 1043 #edb/ref 17592186444621 13194139534928 17592186045417 true] [17592186444600 1043 #edb/ref 17592186444622 13194139534928 17592186045417 true] [17592186444600 1043 #edb/ref 17592186444623 13194139534928 17592186045417 true] [17592186444600 1043 #edb/ref 17592186444624 13194139534928 17592186045417 true] [17592186444600 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534928 17592186045417 true] [17592186444600 1045 "Flux in Three-Dimensional Vector Fields" 13194139534928 17592186045417 true] [17592186444600 1046 #edb/ref 17592186444620 13194139534928 17592186045417 true] [17592186444600 1048 #edb/ref 17592186046660 13194139534928 17592186045417 true] [17592186444600 1049 #edb/ref 17592186050188 13194139534928 17592186045417 true] [17592186444600 1053 #uuid "0bdff687-f8d4-5855-9373-b5ab9e4534b8" 13194139534928 17592186045417 true] [17592186444601 1080 "2" 13194139534928 17592186045417 true] [17592186444601 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534928 17592186